  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Justice and Peace Actors as catalysts of change</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to improve food security and catalyse the peace building and advocacy work of the diocese of Maralal, Kenya.

CAFOD has funded the diocese of Maralal, to implement a 3 year Integrated Food Security Project. The Integrated Food security programme includes, interventions on peace building, governance and advocacy with a focus on holding the county government of Samburu to account. 

In the peace building component, annual community dialogue meetings will be held in conflict prone locations, coupled with training for the farmer groups on peace building. Peace clubs will also be formed in schools and supported to hold inter-school drama and debating activities on peace. The project will further recruit community advocacy agents among the farmer groups, who will be trained and facilitated to undertake public expenditure monitoring at county level. The project will also establish a county liaison desk to be manned by the diocesan county liaison officer and a media strategy will be used to promote accountability through public information sharing.</narrative>
  </description>
